  "query_preview": "..\n\nRest of Today through Friday...\n\nA warm and dry weather pattern is advertised for the northern\nRockies through the weekend and most likely through the work week\nahead. A zonal to slight ridging pattern will be over the area \nfor the next 7 to 8 days. The main storm track/jet stream will \nsettle well to the north of the area, but will be close enough to \npush a few weak and dry cold fronts through the area. Ahead of the\nfronts temperatures will be 15 to 20 degrees above normal (mid \n60s), while post frontal temperatures will still be above normal. \n\nAfter highs in the 75-85 degree range today, a dry cold front\ntonight will bring northerly winds and temperatures near 70 for\nSaturday afternoon. Temperatures warm Sunday into the mid 70s.\nMonday looks very warm with highs well into the 80s, with \n20-40% chance for a 90 degree reading or two east of Billings.\nCould be close to daily high temperature records for a few\nlocations Monday afternoon. Temperatures drop into the upper \n70s/lower 80s behind another dry cold front for Tuesday through \nFriday. \n\nGiven the warm temperatures over the coming week, expect strong\nafternoon mixing to produce breezy to locally windy conditions at\ntimes during the warmest part of each afternoon. \n\nThe combination of warm, dry, and breezy conditions will bring\nperiods of elevated fire weather conditions through next week.\nWill need to use extra caution to prevent grass fires until\na cooler and wetter weather pattern develops. Chambers",
